INT. HAPPY PAWS VET CLINIC - NIGHT

CLOSE ON a keypad. A gloved finger types four numbers. A light turns green. CLICK.

The front door swings open. The clinic is dark and empty, except for the soft glow of a fish tank and a sleeping beagle in a cage.

AIDEN, 20s, in a black hoodie, leads the way. Behind them comes SASHA, 20s, they/them, carrying a duffel bag, and MARLON, 30s, nervous, carrying a flashlight that he keeps pointing at his own face.

AIDEN
(whispering)
Marlon, the light.

MARLON
Sorry. Sorry.

WE SEE the three of them cross the waiting room. Aiden checks a hand-drawn map. Sasha stops at the fish tank and taps the glass, and Marlon trips on a chew toy that SQUEAKS loudly, and the beagle lifts its head, and all three freeze.

ANGLE ON the beagle. It looks at them. It yawns. It goes back to sleep.

SASHA
They're not even mad.

AIDEN
Good. The safe is in Dr. Okafor's office. Down the hall, second door.

MARLON
Why would a vet clinic have a safe?

AIDEN
Because Okafor keeps the old man's ring in it. The one worth sixty thousand dollars.

SASHA
You mean the ring he's been telling everyone is his dead wife's.

AIDEN
Which it isn't. He bought it from the jeweler's two weeks after she left him. I have the receipt.

MARLON
So we're not stealing it. We're, like, returning it.

SASHA
To who?

MARLON
To the universe.

SASHA
That is the worst plan I have ever heard, and I helped build the plan.

AIDEN
Shh. Both of you.

They move down the hall. Aiden pushes a door open, and Sasha slips inside. Marlon waits at the threshold with the flashlight pointing at the floor like a good boy.

INT. DR. OKAFOR'S OFFICE - CONTINUOUS

CLOSE ON the safe. A small grey box behind a framed diploma.

Sasha works the dial with a stethoscope pressed against the metal. Aiden holds the flashlight steady. Marlon stands in the door and watches the hall.

SASHA
(whispering)
Twelve. Twenty-six. Three.

CLICK.

The safe swings open. Inside, on a velvet cushion, sits a small box.

INSERT - THE BOX. Sasha opens it. Inside is a plain gold ring and a folded note.

Aiden unfolds the note and reads.

AIDEN
(quietly)
"If you are reading this, you found out I never told her I was sorry."

Silence. Sasha takes the note, reads it, and passes it to Marlon.

MARLON
I don't think we should take it.

AIDEN
Neither do I.

SASHA
Put it back.

Aiden closes the box. Places it in the safe. Spins the dial. They tiptoe out of the office as the front door CREAKS and a flashlight beam sweeps across the waiting room.

DR. OKAFOR (O.S.)
Hello?

BACK TO SCENE

The three of them freeze in the hallway. Aiden puts a finger to his lips. The beagle barks once.

DR. OKAFOR, 60s, in a raincoat, steps into the beam. He sees them.

DR. OKAFOR
You found it.

AIDEN
We put it back.

DR. OKAFOR
(after a long moment)
Good. Come in and have some tea.
